+# Private Patchright provider
+
+This workstation uses the official `agent-browser` package installed globally with pnpm. Patchright is an independently versioned, private browser provider loaded from the local `agent-browser-priv` checkout. It does not replace the CLI, alter the normal Chrome default, or require npm publication.
+
+## Current registration
+
+The provider is registered globally in `~/.agent-browser/config.json` with this effective configuration:
+
+```text
+Name: patchright
+Command: npx
+Args: -y file:/Users/liuwen/work/agent-browser-priv/packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright
+Capabilities: browser.provider
+```
+
+Inspect it without exposing unrelated configuration:
+
+```bash
+agent-browser plugin show patchright
+```
+
+The `file:` registration resolves the package from the working tree on every provider launch. Keep that checkout on a branch containing `packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright`, and rebuild its `dist/` output after pulling provider changes. Normal updates do not require re-registration.
+
+## Use Patchright explicitly
+
+Prefer the standard Chrome path for ordinary work. Use Patchright when detection-sensitive discovery benefits from its browser launch behavior:
+
+```bash
+agent-browser --provider patchright --headed open https://example.com
+agent-browser snapshot -i
+agent-browser close
+```
+
+Named sessions must repeat the provider only on the command that launches the browser. Always close the exact session when finished:
+
+```bash
+SESSION="$(agent-browser session id --scope worktree --prefix patchright-discovery)"
+agent-browser --session "$SESSION" --provider patchright --headed open https://example.com
+agent-browser --session "$SESSION" snapshot -i
+agent-browser --session "$SESSION" close
+```
+
+The provider uses an existing Google Chrome installation by default. To use Patchright-managed Chromium instead:
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/liuwen/work/agent-browser-priv
+node packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright/dist/index.js \
+  install chromium
+
+AGENT_BROWSER_PATCHRIGHT_CHANNEL=chromium \
+  agent-browser --provider patchright open https://example.com
+```
+
+## Install or re-register
+
+From the private repository root:
+
+```bash
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm --filter agent-browser-plugin-patchright build
+agent-browser plugin add \
+  "file:$PWD/packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright" \
+  --global
+```
+
+The package is marked `private: true`. Keep using the local `file:` registration instead of publishing it to npm.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- `AGENT_BROWSER_PATCHRIGHT_CHANNEL` selects `chrome` or Patchright-managed `chromium`; the default is `chrome`.
+- `AGENT_BROWSER_PATCHRIGHT_RUNTIME_DIR` overrides the private runtime directory; the default is `~/.agent-browser/providers/patchright`.
+- `AGENT_BROWSER_PATCHRIGHT_MAX_LIFETIME_MS` controls forced instance expiry; accepted values range from one minute through seven days and the default is one day.
+
+Each launch creates a fresh temporary profile. The current provider contract does not support extensions or existing profiles.
+
+## Architecture boundary
+
+The provider launches a persistent Chromium context through Patchright, starts a detached supervisor, and returns a browser-level loopback CDP endpoint. Agent-browser then uses its Rust raw-CDP client for snapshots and interaction.
+
+This preserves Patchright's launch arguments and browser selection, but not every native Patchright stealth property. In particular, Patchright's driver-level avoidance of `Runtime.enable` does not apply to agent-browser's CDP client. This provider is useful for agent-browser-driven discovery; it is not equivalent to native Patchright and is not a CAPTCHA or access guarantee.
+
+Use native Patchright directly in a sandbox when the target requires full Patchright driver behavior. Consider other agent-browser providers when a remote browser, managed session, proxy fleet, or provider-specific anti-detection stack is a better fit.
+
+## Cleanup and diagnosis
+
+First close the exact agent-browser session. To request cleanup of all reachable provider-owned instances:
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/liuwen/work/agent-browser-priv
+node packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright/dist/index.js cleanup
+```
+
+Inspect runtime residue only after sessions are closed:
+
+```bash
+find ~/.agent-browser/providers/patchright -type f -print 2>/dev/null
+ps ax -o pid=,command= |
+  rg '[a]gent-browser-plugin-patchright.*__supervise' || true
+```
+
+Do not delete a profile while its supervisor may still be active. The cleanup command intentionally retains ownership records when it cannot authenticate or reach a supervisor.
