+# Upgrade guide
+
+The official CLI, private provider, and Skillbread skill have separate update cycles. Upgrade and verify them in that order.
+
+## 1. Upgrade the official CLI
+
+The official npm package is installed globally through pnpm, not Homebrew and not the private fork:
+
+```bash
+pnpm update -g agent-browser
+agent-browser --version
+which -a agent-browser
+pnpm bin -g
+```
+
+To pin a known release:
+
+```bash
+pnpm add -g agent-browser@<version>
+```
+
+Confirm the first `agent-browser` on `PATH` is under pnpm's global bin directory. If Homebrew appears first, remove the stale Homebrew formula or fix `PATH` before continuing.
+
+## 2. Update and rebuild the private provider
+
+The global plugin configuration points to the local checkout, so keep the checkout on the provider branch and rebuild after pulling changes:
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/liuwen/work/agent-browser-priv
+git switch refactor/patchright-provider
+git pull --ff-only
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm --filter agent-browser-plugin-patchright build
+pnpm --filter agent-browser-plugin-patchright test
+```
+
+No re-registration is normally needed because `~/.agent-browser/config.json` uses a local `file:` reference. Re-register only if the checkout path or plugin entry changes:
+
+```bash
+agent-browser plugin add \
+  "file:$PWD/packages/@agent-browser/plugin-patchright" \
+  --global
+```
+
+## 3. Run a provider smoke test
+
+```bash
+agent-browser plugin show patchright
+
+agent-browser --session patchright-upgrade-smoke \
+  --provider patchright open https://example.com
+agent-browser --session patchright-upgrade-smoke get title
+agent-browser --session patchright-upgrade-smoke snapshot -i
+agent-browser --session patchright-upgrade-smoke close
+```
+
+After closing the session, check for unexpected residue:
+
+```bash
+find ~/.agent-browser/providers/patchright -type f -print 2>/dev/null
+ps ax -o pid=,command= |
+  rg '[a]gent-browser-plugin-patchright.*__supervise' || true
+```
+
+## 4. Refresh the Skillbread skill from official upstream
+
+Skillbread is the source of truth for the user-level skill:
+
+```text
+/Users/liuwen/work/foundation/skillbread/skills/agent-browser
+```
+
+The installed path `~/.agents/skills/agent-browser` must remain a symlink to that directory. Never edit the installed symlink view directly.
+
+To refresh:
+
+1. Fetch the latest `vercel-labs/agent-browser` upstream and copy `skill-data/core/` into Skillbread's `skills/agent-browser/` as the new vendor baseline.
+2. Save the clean official baseline with `just vendor-snapshot agent-browser` before applying local changes.
+3. Reapply `skill-data/patches/skillbread-agent-browser.patch` from the private repository.
+4. Resolve expected upstream drift, keeping the private provider section visibly separate from official guidance.
+5. Update the snapshot metadata in `skills.json`.
+6. Validate and reinstall from the Skillbread root:
+
+```bash
+cd /Users/liuwen/work/foundation/skillbread
+just validate
+just doctor
+just install
+```
+
+Confirm the installed link afterward:
+
+```bash
+readlink ~/.agents/skills/agent-browser
+```
+
+The durable patch is maintained in `/Users/liuwen/work/agent-browser-priv/skill-data/patches/`. Regenerate it from the clean vendor snapshot and customized Skillbread tree whenever the official skill changes.
